    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`solution.py` now implements `encode` and `decode` as the spec describes, and the test suite in `tests/test_solution.py` passes: `python -m pytest -q tests` reports 60 passed.\n\n`encode` groups maximal runs with `itertools.groupby`. Runs of four or more become `~n~c`, other `~` characters are doubled, and everything else is written as-is. `decode` scans left to right and raises `ValueError` for every malformed case in the spec: a trailing `~`, a non-digit after `~`, a count with a leading zero, a count below 4, a count not followed by `~`, and a missing character. It also accepts well-formed text the encoder would not produce, such as plain `aaaa` and adjacent runs. I kept the given signatures and added one private helper, `_read_count`, to parse counts. The tests cover spec examples, every error case, the threshold values 3 and 4, and a seeded round-trip check over random strings. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, so those are unverified.",
